    "https://jobs.ugent.be/job/Gent-Sales-Officer-9000/1375970357/": {
      "title": "Sales Officer Functiedetails",
      "description": "Sales Officer Functiedetails | Universiteit Gent Wij gebruiken cookies om u de best mogelijke website-ervaring te bieden. Uw cookievoorkeuren worden opgeslagen in het lokale geheugen van uw browser. Dit omvat cookies die noodzakelijk zijn voor de werking van de website. Daarnaast kunt u op elk gewenst moment zelf bepalen of u de prestatieverbeteringscookies en cookies die worden gebruikt om inhoud af te stemmen op uw interesses in- of uitschakelt. Accepteert u cookies niet, dan is dit mogelijk van invloed op uw gebruikservaring van de website en de diensten die wij aanbieden. Voorkeuren voor cookies wijzigen Alle cookies afwijzen Alle cookies accepteren Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Mijn profiel JOBS Docenten, hoofddocenten en (gewoon) hoogleraren Assistenten, praktijkassistenten en doctor-assistenten Onderzoekers Bursalen Administratie, ICT, management, techniek en logistiek TechTransfer en het Industrieel Onderzoeksfonds (economische valorisatie) Ghent University Global Campus (Korea) WERKEN BIJ DE UGENT VEELGESTELDE VRAGEN INTERNE VACATURES Taal English Nederlands Mijn profiel JOBS Docenten, hoofddocenten en (gewoon) hoogleraren Assistenten, praktijkassistenten en doctor-assistenten Onderzoekers Bursalen Administratie, ICT, management, techniek en logistiek TechTransfer en het Industrieel Onderzoeksfonds (economische valorisatie) Ghent University Global Campus (Korea) WERKEN BIJ DE UGENT VEELGESTELDE VRAGEN INTERNE VACATURES Taal English Nederlands Mijn profiel JOBS Docenten, hoofddocenten en (gewoon) hoogleraren Assistenten, praktijkassistenten en doctor-assistenten Onderzoekers Bursalen Administratie, ICT, management, techniek en logistiek TechTransfer Office en het Industrieel Onderzoeksfonds (economische valorisatie) Ghent University Global Campus (Zuid-Korea) WERKEN BIJ DE UGENT VEELGESTELDE VRAGEN INTERNE VACATURES Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Personeelscategorie Alle Faculteit / Centrale administratie Alle Tewerkstellingspercentage Alle Locatie Alle Wissen Op de hoogte blijven van ons nieuw aanbod?                 Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) u een melding van nieuwe vacatures wil ontvangen Alert maken × Op de hoogte blijven van ons nieuw aanbod?                 Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) u een melding van nieuwe vacatures wil ontvangen Solliciteer nu » Sales Officer Job ID: 30466 →  Solliciteren tot 03-11-2026 23:59 (Brussels time) →  Faculteit Farmaceutische Wetenschappen →  Vakgroep: FW01 - Geneesmiddelenleer →  Tewerkstellingspercentage: 80% →  Aantal posities: 1 →  Type tewerkstelling: Contract van bepaalde tijd →  Duur van de opdracht: →  Geboden barema:  WM1 tot WM4 of PD1 tot PD4 (masterdiploma of doctoraatsdiploma) →  Diplomavoorwaarde: Master of PhD ABOUT GHENT UNIVERSITY Ghent University is a world of its own. Employing more than 15,000 people, it is actively involved in education and research, management and administration, as well as technical and social service provision on a daily basis. It is one of the largest, most exciting employers in the area and offers great career opportunities. With its 11 faculties and more than 80 departments offering state-of-the-art study programmes grounded in research in a wide range of academic fields, Ghent University is a logical choice for its staff and students. ABOUT CESPE AND CORE FACILITIES The Centre of Excellence in Sustainable Pharmaceutical Engineering and Manufacturing (CESPE) at Ghent University drives innovation in (bio)pharmaceutical production, uniting 15+ research groups and numerous industry partners to advance sustainable, resilient, and efficient manufacturing technologies. The CESPE Innovation Accelerator in The Nucleus building on Eiland Zwijnaarde provides a state-of-the-art environment and infrastructure for research. The Nucleus also hosts two of Ghent University’s Core Facilities (CF) – Drug Product Development core facility (DPD CF), focusing on innovations in pharmaceutical technology and engineering, and HighTru core facility, Belgium’s unique open-access academic high-throughput experimentation (HTE) facility. Core Facilities are organisational units within the university that provide access to infrastructure and equipment, along with the necessary expertise and services. To complement each other’s capabilities, the two facilities have partnered together with a third CF: the NanoMedicine Core (NMC) at the Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences. NMC specialises in nucleic acid delivery systems, by providing end-to-end services for lipid nanoparticle (LNP) development: production, physico-chemical and biological evaluation. The combined infrastructure thus includes a wide range of equipment used for automated chemical synthesis, drug product manufacturing, spectroscopic analysis, physico-chemical and material characterisation, and biological evaluation. To support the market uptake of all 3 core facilities and expand the use of the available equipment by actors outside of the Ghent University, CESPE is looking for a Sales Officer. In this role, you will collaborate on a daily basis with the CESPE General Manager and Core Facility & Lab Managers. JOB DESCRIPTION: SALES OFFICER As Sales Officer, you will serve as the single commercial point of contact across three Ghent University Core Facilities: the Drug Product Development core facility (DPD), the NanoMedicine Core (NMC), and the HighTru core facility. Your key responsibilities will be: Single point of contact for industry: Act as the central contact for all industrial inquiries across DPD, NMC, and HighTru, ensuring a consistent and professional interface with external partners. Customer relationship management (CRM): Create a central CRM overview of all ongoing and potential industrial interactions across the three facilities, enabling systematic relationship continuity. Lead generation and market outreach: Proactively identify market needs and generate qualified leads through networking, sector intelligence, (international) conference presence, and targeted outreach to pharma and biotech companies in Belgium, Benelux, and beyond. For HighTru, building new markets for novel capabilities will be necessary, which requires going beyond just managing existing relationships. Proposal preparation and deal closure: Support the conversion of leads into larger collaborations by preparing tailored proposals, negotiating terms, and coordinating with scientific teams throughout the process, from initial discussions to contract finalisation.. Platform cross-selling: Systematically map what each industrial contact already uses across the three facilities, identify adjacent services relevant to their pipeline, and introduce them to the full platform offering. This includes coordinating across multiple autonomous academic entities with distinct leadership. Market intelligence: Act as the platform's market intelligence function by regularly consolidating observations on pricing, competitor activity, emerging client needs, and R&D trends, and translating these into actionable recommendations for facility managers to support cost model updates, service portfolio decisions, and investment priorities in an anticipatory manner. . Communication and reporting: Coordinate quotations, reporting templates, and marketing materials; liaise with relevant Business Developers within Ghent University for institutional business development support. Desired education and professional experience: Education : You hold an MSc in pharmaceutical sciences, biochemistry, chemistry, biomedical sciences, or a related discipline. A PhD degree is an asset but not required. Knowledge of nanomedicines, formulation science, or synthetic chemistry is a strong advantage. A basic understanding of the technologies is required to communicate effectively with potential clients. Commercial experience: You have demonstrated experience or a strong interest in business development, account management, CRO/CDMO sales, or building a BD pipeline from early stage is an advantage. You are able to structure proposals, negotiate agreements, and close deals. Ideally, you maintain a continued connection to industry (e.g., part-time industry employment alongside this position). Scientific communication: You can translate complex scientific capabilities into industry-relevant value propositions and are confident presenting at scientific and business forums. Relationship management: You have a proactive, persistent follow-up culture and CRM discipline. You are able to maintain and develop relationships across long sales cycles with procurement managers, R&D leads, and scientific staff alike. Regulatory awareness: Basic familiarity with the pharmaceutical regulatory context (IND, GMP, ICH Q guidelines) is a plus, given the GMP-adjacent nature of some services that CF’s offer. Language skills: You are fluent in English (C1 level or equivalent). Dutch is a strong advantage for Belgian industrial engagement. Ecosystem knowledge: You have knowledge of or experience with the inner workings of universities and industrial actors such as pharmaceutical and biotech companies. An existing relevant network is a major plus. Communication and teamwork: You are a strong communicator, both verbal and written, and a team player who can work independently in a structured manner within a complex academic environment. You have a proactive \"get things done\" attitude. WHAT WE OFFER We offer you an 80% part-time contract for MSc degree holders and 60% part-time contract for PhD degree holders. Your contract will start on 31/12/2026 at the latest. Your remuneration will be determined by salary scale WM1 to WM4 (if you hold a Master’s degree) or salary scale PD1 to PD4 (if you hold a doctorate). Click here for more information about our salary scales . All Ghent University staff members enjoy a number of benefits, such as a wide range of training and education opportunities, 36 days of holiday leave (on an annual basis for a full-time job) supplemented by annual fixed bridge days, bicycle allowance and eco vouchers. Click here for a complete overview of all the staff benefits (in Dutch). INTERESTED? Apply online through the e-recruitment system before the application deadline (see above). We do not accept late applications or applications that are not submitted through the online system. Your application must include the following documents: In the field ‘CV’ : your CV and an overview of your study results (merged into one pdf file) In the field ‘Cover letter’ : your application letter in pdf format In the field ‘Diploma’ : a transcript of the required degree (if already in your possession). If you have a foreign diploma in a language other than our national languages (Dutch, French or German) or English, please add a translation in one of the mentioned languages. In the field “other documents”: a reference letter, an overview of your study results,  … Note that the maximum file size for each field is 10 MB. As Ghent University maintains an equal opportunities and diversity policy, everyone is encouraged to apply for this position. MORE INFORMATION For more information about this vacancy, please contact Willem Dhooge ( willem.dhooge@ugent.be ) Important: do NOT send your application by email, but apply online. Heb je vragen over online solliciteren? Lees de FAQ of contacteer ons via selecties@ugent.be. Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke jobs: Onderzoekers selecties@ugent.be FAQ Privacyverklaring Cookies beheren Cookieverklaring UGent Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. © UGent | Sint-Pietersnieuwstraat 25 | 9000 Gent × Beheer - cookies toestaan Als u een website bezoekt, wordt er mogelijk informatie in uw browser opgeslagen of opgehaald. Het gaat hier vooral om cookies. Omdat we uw recht op privacy respecteren, kunt u ervoor kiezen om bepaalde cookies niet